From 8487dba52b85b484b8f95db78d920a5da8243168 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 14:26:10 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-69: the CSV table laid out in VS Code -- style-src
 'unsafe-inline' (0.69.0)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

EastSun's screenshot of IO_Table.csv (1125 rows x 15 columns read, but every
column name piled up in the top-left corner and no row in sight): "哭 你這樣
要我怎麼改?". The table places every cell with style="left:...;top:..." (only
the rows in sight are drawn), and the webview's CSP had style-src without
'unsafe-inline' -- VS Code drops those attributes, so every cell landed at the
same place. The headless test page had no CSP, so it passed.
- the table's CSP: style-src <webview source> 'unsafe-inline'
- the headless test page now has the same style-src policy, and checks the
  layout: columns side by side, rows one under the other, the header above
  (with the old policy the same page gives every cell 0,41 -- checked once by
  hand: layoutOk false)
- smoke: the CSV webview's CSP has 'unsafe-inline' in style-src

Tests: all 4 layers pass (lib 153, smoke 156, real VS Code 141).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
